# Context module

this PR mainly changes the behaviour of `@equinor/fusion-react-legacy-interopt`, but also has some minor tweaks to the `@equinor/fusion-module-context`, which aligns `setContext` with observable (see breaking changes)

this PR main moves logic from the `ContextSelector` component into the registration of legacy application loading (which the `@equinor/fusion-react-legacy-interopt` module will create a "fake" `@equinor/fusion-module-context` module if the application has a `context` attribute in their manifest (see `@equinor/fusion-api` `registerApp`)

the framework does __not__ do any routing when context changes, this __must__ be implemented by the portal
> since the portal is set navigate, all portal and applications must comply with the `apps/APP_KEY/CONTEXT_ID` pattern

> __future discussions__
>
> 1. if we allow the application to generate the url, portals that have strict context management might not work as intended
> 2. if we allow application to generate custom url, there are no pattern to route from one portal to another with context
> 3. if the context is part of the `basename`, all existing application which has context routes will break.
> 4. if the context is part of the `basename`, we might get issues with reconcile of the application, since a root property changes and all routes need to be updated

## Loading of applications

```mermaid
---
title: Load Application
---
flowchart
    A(("/app/${APP_KEY}")) --> C{"has render method"}
    C-->|yes|D(("render"))
    C-->|no|C2["create framework render component"]
    C2-->C3["create legacy browser history"]
    C3-->D
```

```mermaid
---
title: Initialize Application (context)
---
flowchart
  b["resolve context"]
    a1((initialize))-->a2["configure"]
    a2-->a3["resolve initial context"]
    a3-->a4{"has context in path"}
    a4-->|yes|b1["resolve context"]
    a4-->|no|c1{"context in localstorage"}
    subgraph legacy app
      c1
    end
    c1-->|no|d1["set context from parent"]
    d1-->|"verify and resolve related"|b1
    c1-->|"verify and resolve related"|b1
    b1-->e1((render))
```


#### default resolver
[see code](https://github.com/equinor/fusion-framework/blob/41d07800c149758337b0e742ed45c658be889d4f/packages/modules/context/src/utils/resolve-initial-context.ts)
```ts
/** default resolver */
const resolveInitialContext =
  (options?: {
      path?: ContextPathResolveArgs;
  }): Required<ContextModuleConfig>['resolveInitialContext'] =>
  ({ ref, modules }) => {
      const { context, navigation } = modules;
      const pathResolver = resolveContextFromPath(context, options?.path);
      return concat(
          /** if navigation mode available, try to resolve from path */
          navigation ? pathResolver(navigation.path.pathname) : EMPTY,
          resolveContextFromParent({ ref, modules })
      ).pipe(first());
};
```

#### Custom resolver for legacy application

```ts
/** legacy app registration */
registerApp('my-app', { 
    AppComponent,
    /** creates context-module based on provided config`*/
    context: {
        types: [ContextTypes.ProjectMaster],
        buildUrl: (context: Context | null, url: string) => {
            if (!context) return '';
            return `/${context.id}`;
        },
        getContextFromUrl: (url: string) => {
            const contextId = url.replace('/', '');
            return contextId.length > 10 ? contextId : '';
        },
    },
});
```
[see complete code](https://github.com/equinor/fusion-framework/blob/41d07800c149758337b0e742ed45c658be889d4f/packages/react/legacy-interopt/src/create-legacy-render.tsx#L74)
```ts
/** snippet from create-legacy-render.tsx */
builder.setResolveInitialContext((args) => {
    const resolver = resolveInitialContext({
        path: contextConfig.getContextFromUrl
            ? {
                  extract: contextConfig.getContextFromUrl,
                  validate: (path: string) => !!path,
              }
            : {
                  validate: (path: string) => {
                      return (
                          /** legacy project id */
                          !!path.match(/^\d+$/) ||
                          !!path.match(/^(?:[a-z0-9]+-){4}[a-z0-9]+$/)
                      );
                  },
              },
    });
    /** sequentially go threw resolvers and stop at first resolved */
    return concat(
        resolver(args),
        /** load from local storage */
        from(legacy.contextManager.getAsync<'current', ContextItem>('current'))
          .pipe(filter((x): x is ContextItem => !!x))
    ).pipe(
        filter((item): item is ContextItem => !!item),
        take(1)
    );
});
```

BREAKING CHANGE:
- [portal need to implement navigation when context changes](https://github.com/equinor/fusion-framework/pull/815/commits/41d07800c149758337b0e742ed45c658be889d4f)
- [current context can now be `null`](https://github.com/equinor/fusion-framework/pull/815/commits/6f7370e990f837cd5409932f3a9b0f964169154a)
- [skipInitialContext is now removed](https://github.com/equinor/fusion-framework/pull/815/commits/62c27dda42021daa7795891d4e831bbc8cc7ccf7)
- [postInitialize no longer support void function, should not affect any application, only used internally](https://github.com/equinor/fusion-framework/pull/815/commits/be8cbdf493baad9c5add5a027626bbbcd9e3c527)
- [`ContextProvider.setCurrentContext` now returns an `Observable`](https://github.com/equinor/fusion-framework/pull/815/commits/cd3036959b7f23936863100c67a997fb07c9ee6c)
- [configurator.postInitialize no longer support void function](https://github.com/equinor/fusion-framework/pull/815/commits/be8cbdf493baad9c5add5a027626bbbcd9e3c527)
